  "details": "Having an enum as an optional argument to a method causes compile errors. The errors show up as `[UdonSharp] Assets/Scripts/Test.cs(12,1): System.ArgumentException: Type provided must be an Enum.` with the code location in the errors being seemingly random and unrelated.\n\nCode to replicate bug:\n\n```\n\nenum AnEnum {\n\n    Option,\n\n    AnotherOption\n\n}\n\npublic class Test : UdonSharpBehaviour\n\n{\n\n    void OptionalEnum(AnEnum anEnum = AnEnum.Option)\n\n    {\n\n        \n\n    }\n\n}\n\n```\n\nChanging `void OptionalEnum(AnEnum anEnum = AnEnum.Option)` to `void OptionalEnum(AnEnum anEnum)` removes the errors.",
